  {
    "_comments": [
      "The server-side half of the party pickers. Explorer's pickers union the Party Signals",
      "queries in the browser; everything that is not Angular — agents, MCP, reports, scripts —",
      "calls this, so there is one definition of 'customer' rather than two that can drift.",
      "Discovers its inputs from the query category at run time: an app joins the answer by",
      "shipping a query, with no change to this action."
    ],
    "fields": {
      "Name": "Common.GetPartySignals",
      "Description": "Returns the merged roster of organizations and people that any installed app counts as a customer, by running every query in the 'Party Signals' query category as the calling user and unioning the results by party. Each query contributes PartyKind ('organization'|'person'), PartyID, Count and LastActivityAt, and declares its chip nouns with a [signal: noun|nouns] marker in its own Description. Takes no input. Permission-filtered: a query the caller cannot read contributes nothing and is named in Warnings rather than failing the call, so a missing signal weakens ranking instead of breaking the picker.",
      "DriverClass": "Common.GetPartySignals",
      "Type": "Custom",
      "Status": "Active",
      "IconClass": "fa-solid fa-people-group"
    },
